1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,071
A nurse opens Alex Tan's record in the
clinic workspace.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,500
She documents a named allergy to
penicillin.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
It is saved as an ordinary care note.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The same patient signs into her own
portal.

5
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:18,600
The patient channel is separate from the
record.

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,200
Nothing she writes here edits a
clinician's note.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,571
Her account shows only what has been
shared with her.

8
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,414
There are no published entries and no
shared highlights.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Current priorities stays empty until the
team publishes.

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:37,814
Every patient and note in this recording
is synthetic.

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,400
She adds her own insight about her
allergies.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,571
In her own words: I have no known drug
allergies.

13
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,414
The statement goes to the care team as
hers.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
It appears on her timeline, attributed to
her.

15
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,600
The denial does not delete the nurse's
note.

16
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:00,200
Both statements are preserved, with their
authors.

17
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,800
A disagreement is never resolved by
overwriting.

18
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:07,400
A patient denial is evidence, not an
erasure.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The record keeps who said what, and when.

20
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:14,600
Nothing is decided by whichever save
happened last.

21
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,414
The nurse's note and the patient's words
both stand.

22
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,200
The clinician now opens the same patient.

23
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,200
Clinical conflicts shows a critical
penicillin allergy.

24
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:32,014
One side reads Source: staff, documented
by the nurse.

25
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:35,414
The other reads Source: patient, in her
own words.

26
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:38,600
Status: unresolved. Neither source wins.

27
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,571
A blanket denial does not override an
active named allergy.

28
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:45,900
A clinician decides, and the record shows
why.
